  "body": "Stacked on #135 (issue/103-turning-axial-rapids). Retarget to main before #135 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **#109:** an op whose rapid verdict reads earlier ops now digests the ops ahead into its generation stamp. That covers verify's prior acquittal (`acquit_by_prior` / `PriorPlan`), the drill prior, and #103's lathe pilot and facing credit; the set is `drill_prior::reads_prior`, matching `job::collect_job`. Editing and regenerating, deleting or reordering an earlier op marks the dependent op Stale, the reason names the op that moved, and the post refuses it. 3+2-posed ops keep their stamps.\n- **#145:** Regenerate All runs in rounds. Each round generates every Stale op in program order, writes the results so the next round sees them, and stops when nothing is Stale (capped at the op count; leftovers are reported in `skipped()`). The world is restored after the batch is built and `apply` replays it, so it stays one undo unit. Note that building the batch writes to the world briefly, which is main-thread only (recorded in RECOMMENDED.md).\n- The `turning_bore` fixture moved to `tests/common/bore.rs` (the suite was over 400 lines); `stamp.rs` is 399.\n- **One-time effect:** every non-first op (not 3+2-posed) of a saved project reads Stale once after upgrading.\n\n## Pins\n\n- `vertical_rapid_stock::a_face_regenerated_shallower_marks_the_acquitted_contour_stale`: fails before the fix\n- `turning_bore::a_pilot_deleted_or_made_shallower_after_the_bore_marks_it_stale`: fails before the fix\n- `vertical_rapid_stock::one_regenerate_all_brings_a_dependent_pair_current`: fails without the rounds (`left: 1, right: 2`)\n- `regenerate_all_fixes_the_whole_job_in_one_undo_unit` is back to one round; `threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit` now compares against a sequential generate-and-apply loop.\n\n## Readings\n\nGreen after the merge of #135's tip: turning_bore 11, vertical_rapid_stock 6, operations 117 (6 ignored), remachining 6. Green before it: commands_undo 30, tool_after_state 5, drill_prior 10, drill_prior_kinds 4, posting 17, golden_cl 23, plus the ui `regenerate_all_*` tests and the status-bar test. Clippy on app and ui is clean.\n\nChangelog: an op whose rapid verdict reads earlier ops (prior acquittal, lathe pilot/facing credit) goes Stale when an earlier op of its setup is regenerated, deleted or reordered, and the post refuses it until regenerated; one Regenerate All brings such jobs current in one undo step; one-time: every non-first op (not 3+2-posed) of a saved project reads Stale once after upgrading\n\nFixes #109\nFixes #145\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
